Despite the recent absence of the DevTeam, we are living in a golden age
of patches. Therefore, I have combined some of the more interesting ones
into what should probably be described as a variant, but since I have no
intention of maintaining it, I'll simply call it Super Slightly Less
Added Stuff Hack: Extra Monkeys.

http://james.lab6.com/2006/nethack/sslashem.diff.gz

There are 61 patches included altogether, and before you say "SLASH'EM's
thattaway -->", I would like to claim that I have been quite conservative
in patch selection. There are no firearms, no million-zorkmid
super-artifacts, no monsters named after spice girls -- in fact no new
monsters, branches, roles, techniques or anything like that. The patches
mostly improve the interactions of existing features rather than add new
ones.

Two catches:

1) There are actually no extra monkeys.
2) I made this ages ago, and was only prompted to make it available
because some people seemed to like GruntHack. This means the only
documentation I have for it is this list of patches:

